    "description": "Notion | Send a file upload
Step 2: transfer the bytes for an upload created by \`API-create-a-file-upload\`. Because this server runs remotely and shares no filesystem with the caller, the \`file\` parameter accepts a data: URI, a bare base64 string, or an http(s) URL the server can fetch — a local path only works when running over stdio. Whichever form is used, the whole file travels in this one call as a single unbroken payload: contents produced in pieces must be joined before they are sent, and \`content_length\` is what proves none went missing.
Returns:
A file upload object. It is \`pending\` until the bytes arrive and \`uploaded\` afterwards, and it expires at \`expiry_time\` (one hour) unless it is attached to a block, page property or comment before then.
