  {
    "description": "Notion | Update a view
Change a view's name, filter, sorts, quick filters or layout. Every field is optional and anything omitted is left as it was, so a partial update is safe. To remove a setting, send it as \`null\` — \`filter: null\` drops the filter, \`configuration: {"type": "table", "group_by": null}\` ungroups a table. Sending a \`quick_filters\` entry replaces just that one and leaves the rest; setting an entry to \`null\` removes it. \`configuration.type\` must match the view's existing type. Note that re-applying grouping resets \`hide_empty_groups\` to true, so set it explicitly to false in the same call if empty groups must stay visible.
Error Responses:
400: Bad request",
